{% if dev_in_worktrees %}
### Quick Setup For Development

There is no main Odoo, no Nginx and no main database in development: every pipeline
run (one task, or a block of tasks) runs in its own worktree env (`.claude/skills/worktree-env`), with its own Odoo on
its own port and its own restore of the prod dump in the shared PostgreSQL cluster.

This will:

1. Create `.env` file with configuration
1. Clone/update all repositories
1. Initialize the PostgreSQL cluster and its service
{% if backup_s3_bucket %}
1. Configure AWS credentials (for the prod dump)
{% endif %}
{% if prod_ssh_host %}
1. Setup SSH access for servers
{% endif %}
{% if editor == 'vscode' %}
1. Create VSCode settings
{% endif %}

```bash
cd {{ project_name }}

# Run full setup
nix run .#setup-dev

# Lock python dependencies from src/odoo/requirements.txt
nix run .#bootstrap-deps

# INSTALL PERMANENTLY TO YOUR SYSTEM
{% if service_suffix %}mkdir -p ~/.local/state/nix/profiles && {% endif %}nix profile add {{ nix_profile_flag }}.#dev-server

# The PostgreSQL cluster every worktree env's database lives in
systemctl --user enable --now postgres{{ service_suffix }}.service
{% if backup_s3_bucket %}

# Fetch the newest prod dump into backup/ (each worktree env restores its own copy)
nix run .#download-backup
{% endif %}

# A worktree env per pipeline run: start (idempotent), list, stop
bash .claude/skills/worktree-env/scripts/wt-start.sh <slug>     # prints URL, CONF, DB, PORT
bash .claude/skills/worktree-env/scripts/wt-start.sh <slug> --env-repo   # + this repo on branch <slug>
bash .claude/skills/worktree-env/scripts/wt-list.sh
bash .claude/skills/worktree-env/scripts/wt-stop.sh <slug>

# Logs:
tail -f ${{ project_dir_var }}/.postgres/log/postgresql.log | ccze -A
tail -f ${{ project_dir_var }}/.worktrees/_env/<slug>/odoo.log | ccze -A

# Odoo update module / shell on a session:
{{ odoo_cmd }} -c ${{ project_dir_var }}/.worktrees/_env/<slug>/odoo.conf -u module_name --workers 0 --stop-after-init --logfile=
{{ odoo_cmd }} shell -c ${{ project_dir_var }}/.worktrees/_env/<slug>/odoo.conf --workers 0 --no-http

# Tests on a session (free port, IPv4 loopback for HttpCase, a dbfilter naming its DB):
bash .claude/skills/worktree-env/scripts/wt-test.sh <slug> -u module_name --test-enable --test-tags /module_name
{% if prod_ssh_host %}

# Connect to remote servers:
{% if test_ssh_hosts %}
test-server <alias>     # one of: {{ test_ssh_hosts | join(', ') }}
{% endif %}
prod-server
{% endif %}

# help message with all commands and URLs:
welcome-message
```

